Client & Server

Socho tum ek workshop me ho.
Tumhe kaam karna hai, par tumhare paas tool (axe) nahi hai.

Client:
Tum — jo kaam start karne ke liye axe mang rahe ho.
(In tech: Application, browser, or system sending a request)

Server:
Tool store — jaha axe padhi hai.
Tumhara request aaya → axe tumhe di gayi → tum kaam shuru kar dete ho.
(In tech: Machine or service that processes the request and returns the response)


DevOps Perspective:

Client: Developer ne Jenkins pipeline run ki → request gaya build ke liye.

Server: Jenkins master/agent ne build execute kiya, result pack karke return kiya.


Lesson:
Axe ka sharp, available, aur ready hona utna hi important hai jitna server ka fast aur reliable hona.

Client request fast ho sakti hai, par agar server delay kare to delivery slow ho jayegi.
